    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d93-a2">

                <pb facs="0194" n="132" sameAs="frus:frus1878/pg132"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure to inclosure 1 in No.
                    11.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chamber of Commerce to Mr.
                            Stahel.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1878-05-22"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 22,
                        1878</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt of your letter of 6th instant,
                    inclosing four copies of a memorandum on the currency of China by his excellency
                    the United States minister at Peking.</p>
                <p>The members of the committee have perused the documents with much interest, and
                    the possession of so valuable a record of information, and so clear a statement
                    of the question, will prove most useful to the chamber in considering the
                    subject of which his excellency treats.</p>
                <p>The committee regrets to be forced to the conviction, by the result of recent
                    endeavors to induce the Chinese Government to place the currency of the country
                    on a more satisfactory basis, that there is no present prospect of progress in
                    the matter; but it will, nevertheless, not cease to engage the attention of the
                    chamber, in the hopes that means may ultimately be found of persuading the
                    government to recognize and perform what in western countries is considered the
                    ordinary duty of the state.</p>
                <p>I have to request that you will be kind enough to convey to Mr. Seward the thanks
                    of the chamber for his excellency’s communication.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>F. B. JOHNSON,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Chairman.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
